\image(figures/cora_gcn_fit.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Fitting and held-out likelihood plus held-out accuracy after each of the three updates. The gray line is the accuracy of always predicting the most common held-out class.)
\alttext(Line plots showing fitting and held-out loss, and held-out accuracy compared with a majority-class reference.)

The majority reference uses the held-out class distribution as a descriptive
comparison. It does not influence the optimizer. The fixed graph makes this
a transductive evaluation.

> References

- [Kipf and Welling (2017), Semi-Supervised Classification with Graph Convolutional Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.02907).
- [Original Cora tables from the pinned pygcn mirror](https://github.com/tkipf/pygcn/tree/1600b5b748b3976413d1e307540ccc62605b4d6d/data/cora).
